WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
As the evening gets darker,
street lights flicker on,

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.310
one after another.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.990
Nobody walks round flipping switches.

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.270
Somewhere in each lamp's circuit,

5
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.110
something notices that
the light is fading.

6
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.910
So which part of the circuit
can tell it is getting dark?

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.150
In this mission, you'll read
graphs of current against voltage

8
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.510
for a resistor, a filament
lamp and a diode,

9
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.330
and see why only one of
them gives a straight line.

10
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.510
You'll also meet two components
that respond to the world

11
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.750
around them.

12
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.170
Your mission: find the part of
the circuit that notices the

13
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.150
dark.
